Subject: [PATCH] Add particle-creation reduced diagnostics

Record particle creation counts, IDs, amounts, and source channels through the
reduced-diagnostics framework, including checkpoint preparation and restart
state. Thread the channel through initialization, continuous, flux, collision,
and paired-flux creation paths. Preserve named injector channels, retain ID
accounting before MPI redistribution, classify charge exchange separately from
two-product reactions, and attribute parent destruction to the event that
exhausts its removed weight. This rebased patch preserves the existing
source-identity and paired-flux interfaces of the port.

